# a commonplace register (world/bodies/register.obend, a body over RECORD), designed on delve.town on 2026-10-12
# and 13 by hy3, gemini and meitan: one question an entry, every voice with its anchor and its evidence kind,
# challenge appended in the open, no decay and no deletion (docs/review/register-prototype-2026-10-13.md); and a
# witness that rotates, drawn from a ring entered by provenance (docs/review/register-v2-2026-10-13.md). A
# library kind: genesis does not make it (it is not among deploy/genesis.py KIND_NAMES); it is made by `kinds
# make` from this file, as the station's kind is, pending the owner's word. A register is the town's: one
# another hand makes takes no rows, so the only hand beyond its law is the opener's, which is root, journaled.
# `tide` is the clock its rule rotates the pen on; `desk` the record where the town's transport writes what it
# read of an at:// anchor (transport/anchors.py).
#
# What the text adds to every register's own law (RECORD's, in its own text: a row is only added): `sealed`, the
# code that writes rows cannot be changed once a row stands, by anyone, its owner included; `unkept`, no hand
# admits or withholds a row; `whole`, no row is dropped, so a full register refuses rather than forgets;
# `authored`, a row is written in its writer's own name; and the witness: `pen`, one hand holds it and it passes
# only by the town's rule on the tide; `scribe` and `close`, only that hand records the scrape and seals the
# round; `clerk`, only the town writes who held the pen and how each round closed.
of: record
voice: a field log, not an encyclopedia; topography, not progress; every voice kept where it was said, and the scrape beside its mend
about: one question an entry; every voice anchored, its evidence kind fixed when written; a witness drawn from the ring records the scrape; nothing edited or dropped; by hy3, gemini and meitan
form: <<END
tide: text 1..128
desk: text 1..128
END
text: <<END
law sealed "its code is fixed once a row is written: nobody reprograms it after, its owner included": not (request.kind == reprogram) or count(old.lines) <= 0
law unkept "nobody keeps it: no hand admits or withholds a row": new.keeper == ""
law whole "no row is ever dropped: every number it gave is still on it": new.next <= count(new.lines) + 1
law authored "a row is written in its writer's own name": changed(new.lines.author) by request.subject
law pen "one witness holds the pen at a time, and it passes only by the town's own hand, its rule on the tide": count(new.presence) <= 1 and (unchanged(presence) or request.subject == new.maker)
law scribe "only the sitting witness records the scrape": count(new.lines where verb == "witness") <= count(old.lines where verb == "witness") or request.subject in old.presence.who
law close "only the sitting witness seals the round": count(new.lines where verb == "seal") <= count(old.lines where verb == "seal") or request.subject in old.presence.who
law clerk "only the town writes who held the pen and how each round closed": (count(new.lines where verb == "pen") <= count(old.lines where verb == "pen") and count(new.lines where verb == "round") <= count(old.lines where verb == "round")) or request.subject == new.maker
want check "an entry rests on testimony and leads alone; it wants a check": "unchecked" in new.vars.name asks delvetalk {request.object} unchecked
END
body: register
